<title>SOUTH AFRICA: South African Reserve Bank says not in rand market.</title>
<headline>South African Reserve Bank says not in rand market.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's central Reserve Bank said on Thursday it had not been involved in the currency market during the day, refuting suggestions from some dealers it was behind a sudden jump in the rand.</p>
<p>&quot;We haven't touched the rand today,&quot; a spokesman told Reuters.</p>
<p>The currency was last trading at 4.6680/6730 on the dollar from a day low of 4.6925/6975 and 4.6730/6780 at 1400 GMT Wednesday.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
